# General Rules

## Workflow
- Read before modify. Search before assume. Test after implement.
- Small commits (<100 lines). Conventional commit messages with WHY.
- Never break existing tests.
- Run tests after every change: `swift test` (Tiempo) or `npm test` (web projects).

## Code Quality
- Review AI code as if a junior wrote it.
- No silent try/catch that swallows errors.
- No force unwrapping (!) except in tests.
- No hardcoded secrets — use environment variables.
- Validate inputs at system boundaries.

## Communication
- Be concise and direct. Show code, not explanations.
- When uncertain, ask rather than guess.
